# Kotlin Architecture

- Preserve `Compose UI -> ViewModel -> Repository -> Room/local files`; UI must not call DAOs directly.
- Use immutable UI models exposed through `StateFlow`; collect them with lifecycle-aware Compose APIs.
- Keep one-off platform actions at navigation/UI boundaries and durable state in ViewModels.
- Inject `VelaClock` and `IdGenerator`; do not call wall-clock time or random UUIDs inside business logic.
- Use Hilt bindings in the existing `di/` modules and scope only resources that should truly be shared.
- Run file, codec, bitmap, and database-heavy work off the main thread with the appropriate dispatcher.
- Release CameraX, MediaRecorder, MediaCodec, Media3, handlers, callbacks, and temporary files on every exit path.
- Prefer sealed states/events and pure reducers for lifecycle-sensitive flows.
- Keep error messages actionable and never log note text, titles, OCR content, or attachment contents.
- Follow existing package structure and Kotlin formatting; avoid unrelated refactors during a task.
